zerodce.py is adapted from Zero-DCE++/model.py of https://github.com/Li-Chongyi/Zero-DCE_extension
(commit 09f202b690f82da939b8e6ec8535960ae97ad8bd). The weights (Zero-DCE++/snapshots_Zero_DCE++/Epoch99.pth)
are from the same repository. The repository has no LICENSE file; its README says, verbatim:

    ##  License
    The code is made available for academic research purpose only. Under Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0
    International License.

Attribution: Chongyi Li, Chunle Guo, Chen Change Loy, "Learning to Enhance Low-Light Image via
Zero-Reference Deep Curve Estimation", IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence, 2021,
doi:10.1109/TPAMI.2021.3063604.

License text: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Changes: only the inference parts are kept (the network and the curve); the curve is applied with one map
(the mean of the three) to max(R, G, B), scaled by a strength, and the maps are smoothed over time
(rounds/README.md, Repair). Not for commercial use.
